>> instakilled by poison.
> 
> Well, yes, but he found a /oW on dlvl 1.  And used it for +2 SDSM
> first.  With that and the wizard's starting cloak, he's already in
> that tiny fraction of players who aren't going to be killed by ants,
> jackals or wands, and just might live to ascend.  Assuming they don't
> stumble into a poisoned spiked pit without poison resistance, that is.

His list of wishes:

> #1 2 blessed scroll of charging (get 2)
> #2 blessed greased +2 SDSM  (get +2)
> #3: nothing happens...
> OK, it was (0:2) apparently... Use one scroll of charging.
> #3 (again) 2 blessed tins of Green Dragon meat (thanks to RGRN, as I
> wouldn't have wished for that before reading a recent thread)
> ...
> (wait from some extra Xplvl here)
> ...
> #4 blessed fixed +2 Staff of Aesculapius (really great for neutral
> wizard, I think, both in early and mid-game... and end-game!)
> #5 blessed fixed greased +2 speedboots
> #6 blessed fixed greased +2 gauntlets of dexterity (I started with a
> magic marker, if it weren't the case, I would have probably go for
> one

#3 looks really, really bad in this light.

And waiting to gain more levels before blowing out the wand of wishing
looks just as bad, if not worse.

#5 should have been #3.  Speed boots are a huge survival benefit at
early levels, where most things aren't even 'fast'.  You may want to
switch to jumping later, but you've got a whole game to find a pair.

Then, he waits.  Waiting with the castle wand makes some sense, as few
characters are in danger of immediate death by that point.  But on DL1,
you want to burn out the wand all the way down to the wrest to make sure
you _get_ to the castle.

So, #4 has to happen immediately, otherwise you risk random artifacts
showing up that you don't even see.

#5 could easily have been gauntlets of power or a bag of holding, but
there's a case to be made for GoDex since this is a wizard...
admittedly, not a very good one.

By the time you're down to #6, THEN blessed tins of poison resistance
start to look good... mostly because he started with a marker and is now
getting close to "out of things to wish for", ... though I would
definitely go for the amulet of life saving instead, put that on, kill
the first unicorn I saw (easy to do with that much armor, speed boots,
and the Staff), and then just eat poisonous corpses and unihorn the stat
loss back.

> (Also, early poison resistance has an additional survival advantage:
> it lets you eat poisonous corpses, which helps avoid starvation 

You're kidding, right?  I've never starved with any character once I
left the "raw newbie" stage.  Eat the non-poisonous stuff, #pray if you
get in a tight spot, and do Sokoban first so you get a ton of food rations.

